The labels on the version surface (PAR-SEC-002, an M1 Required row: the build
reports the Chromium version, the patch delta, and the known lag).

Derived one-for-one from `UpstreamProvenance` in
//taffy/resources/branding/taffy_upstream_provenance.h. Each label names a
field; the values themselves are generated from chromium/REVISION,
chromium/SECURITY_PATCH_LEVEL and chromium/patches/ and never appear here.

These are the pak half of the catalogue: they are read by browser-process C++
on the version surface, not by Java. Nothing here is duplicated in the Android
string set, and nothing in the Android set is duplicated here.

Two wordings are load-bearing:

  * "Downstream changes" and "Downstream changed lines" say what the fork has
    actually done to files Chromium owns. A person reading a browser built by
    someone other than Chromium is entitled to that number.
  * The lag row states the date the revision was pinned rather than a number
    of days, because the binary does not know today's date at build time. A
    build with no recorded pin date says so instead of showing a lag it cannot
    support.
-->
<grit-part>
  <message name="IDS_TAFFY_VERSION_SECTION_TITLE"
           desc="Heading of the section on the version page that describes the upstream Chromium revision this build was made from and how far it has been changed.">
    Upstream Chromium
  </message>
  <message name="IDS_TAFFY_VERSION_UPSTREAM_MILESTONE"
           desc="Label for the Chromium milestone number this build was made from, for example 152.">
    Chromium milestone
  </message>
  <message name="IDS_TAFFY_VERSION_UPSTREAM_TAG"
           desc="Label for the full Chromium stable release tag this build was made from, for example 152.0.7977.42.">
    Chromium version
  </message>
  <message name="IDS_TAFFY_VERSION_UPSTREAM_COMMIT"
           desc="Label for the exact upstream Chromium commit this build was made from.">
    Chromium revision
  </message>
  <message name="IDS_TAFFY_VERSION_PIN_RECORDED"
           desc="Label for the date on which this Chromium revision was pinned. A reader compares it with today to judge how far behind upstream this build is.">
    Revision pinned on
  </message>
  <message name="IDS_TAFFY_VERSION_PIN_RECORDED_UNKNOWN"
           desc="Shown in place of the pin date when the build was made outside a source checkout, so the date could not be recorded. Says what is missing rather than showing a lag that cannot be supported.">
    Not recorded in this build
  </message>
  <message name="IDS_TAFFY_VERSION_DOWNSTREAM_PATCHES"
           desc="Label for how many changes TaffyGo applies to files that Chromium owns.">
    Downstream changes
  </message>
  <message name="IDS_TAFFY_VERSION_DOWNSTREAM_PATCH_LINES"
           desc="Label for how many lines of Chromium-owned source TaffyGo changes in total.">
    Downstream changed lines
  </message>
  <message name="IDS_TAFFY_VERSION_SECURITY_PATCH_LEVEL"
           desc="Label for how many urgent upstream security fixes have been applied on top of the pinned revision. Resets to zero each time the build moves to a newer Chromium milestone.">
    Security fixes applied on top
  </message>
  <message name="IDS_TAFFY_VERSION_SECURITY_ADVISORIES"
           desc="Label for the upstream advisory references covered by the security fixes applied on top of the pinned revision.">
    Security references
  </message>
</grit-part>
